  "steps": [
    "Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C). Line a large rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper.",
    "In a small mixing bowl, whisk together the whole grain mustard, honey, olive oil, minced garlic, kosher salt, and black pepper until smooth.",
    "Arrange the salmon fillets down the center of the prepared baking sheet, leaving space on the sides.",
    "Place the trimmed asparagus spears in a single layer on both sides of the salmon.",
    "Brush the honey mustard glaze evenly over the top of each salmon fillet and drizzle the remaining glaze over the asparagus.",
    "Roast in the preheated oven at 400°F (200°C) for 12 to 15 minutes, until the salmon flakes easily with a fork and the asparagus is tender-crisp."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Ensure salmon fillets are of similar thickness so they cook at the exact same rate.",
    "Store leftover cooked salmon and asparagus in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days."
  ],
  "storage": "Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.",
